# Response headers Cloudflare Pages adds to every route of this build.
# Copied to the site root verbatim by Astro, like everything else in public/.
#
# The one policy here is the Content-Security-Policy, added with the ad partner:
# the AdSense tag (src/lib/ads.ts) is the first third-party script this site
# executes, and it runs in this document with full access to it. The allowlist
# below is what stops a compromised or hijacked tag from pulling further code in
# from anywhere it likes. Ad creatives themselves are cross-origin iframes with
# documents - and policies - of their own, so widening this for them is neither
# needed nor possible.
#
# Editing rules:
#   - a NEW third-party script host has to be added to script-src here, and a new
#     embed (a video, a map) to frame-src, or the browser blocks it and the
#     feature silently does nothing;
#   - keep it in step with what the code actually loads: GA4 (analytics.ts) and
#     AdSense (ads.ts) are the only two script origins today, and the ad units are
#     the only frames.
#
# The three headers under the policy are the rest of the baseline, and are here
# for the same reason the policy is - the ad tag puts a third-party frame on the
# page: nosniff stops a response being executed as a type it did not declare,
# Referrer-Policy keeps the path of the page a visitor is reading out of the
# request that fetches an ad (the origin still goes, which is what the partner
# needs), and HSTS keeps this site off plain HTTP for a year. The HSTS is
# deliberately narrow: no `includeSubDomains`, because sibling hosts
# (images.sleekdrops.com, go.sleekdrops.com) are served by other configs this
# file knows nothing about and a year is a long time to break one, and no
# `preload`, because that is a listing that cannot be withdrawn quickly.
#
# 'unsafe-inline' is in script-src because the theme bootstrap in SEOHead.astro
# and the JSON-LD blocks in JsonLd.astro are inline, and a static host cannot
# mint a per-response nonce. connect-src is left at any https origin because the
# analytics and flag-delivery hosts are per-environment build settings
# (PUBLIC_DEVTEAM_ANALYTICS_HOST, PUBLIC_DEVTEAM_FLAGS_HOST) that this static
# file cannot know; script-src, which is what governs code execution, is not
# widened that way.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.googleadservices.com https://*.googletagservices.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://adservice.google.com https://www.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; frame-src https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com; connect-src 'self' https:
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
